TEXT 56 80 Left 2 ;Supply: D1 and C1 are on the 9 V board, R1 C2 C3 on the buffer board
TEXT 56 344 Left 2 ;Guitar stand-in (edit freely)
TEXT 56 488 Left 2 ;VIN: 1 kHz sine, VPK peak, AC 1
TEXT 56 508 Left 2 ;Rsrc, Ccab: pickup and lead
TEXT 392 632 Left 2 ;SW1 Inst/Line toggle, modelled as two resistors
TEXT 392 652 Left 2 ;LINESEL=0 is Inst (x1), LINESEL=1 is Line (-9.7 dB)
TEXT 392 672 Left 2 ;R_SWI is 1m ohm at Inst and 1G at Line; R_SWL is the reverse
TEXT 904 408 Left 2 ;WM8960 board LINPUT1, as it is today
TEXT 904 640 Left 2 ;Not part of the buffer: 100 ohm + 47 nF on the board, then 1 uF
TEXT 904 660 Left 2 ;coupling into the codec, 49 kohm at PGA 0 dB (plan.md, Phase 2b)
TEXT 336 696 Left 2 ;U1B: the spare half, a follower on the bias
TEXT 48 1000 Left 2 ;Bias is VF/3 through R2 R3 R4, with C4 across R4
TEXT 48 16 Left 3 ;Pedal input buffer: OPA2197 follower, Inst/Line pad, bias from the filtered 9 V
TEXT 720 72 Left 2 ;Net names and refs follow pedal.project/stripboard/nets.py; values are docs/bom.md.
TEXT 720 96 Left 2 ;U1A and U1B are one OPA2197. The model is LTspice UniversalOpAmp2 set to its
TEXT 720 120 Left 2 ;headline figures (10 MHz GBW, 20 V/us, 5.5 nV/rtHz), not TI's model. It draws about
TEXT 720 144 Left 2 ;0.4 mA a half from VF, so VF and BIAS move a little with the real part's supply
TEXT 720 168 Left 2 ;current. Swap in TI's OPA2197 model for exact numbers. Input capacitance is not modelled.
TEXT 720 192 Left 2 ;GND is one node here; the pedal has GND_A and GND_P joined at the star.
TEXT 720 728 Left 2 !.param LINESEL=0 VPK=1.4 Rsrc=10k Ccab=500p
TEXT 720 752 Left 2 !.ac dec 50 1 1Meg
TEXT 720 776 Left 2 !.step param LINESEL list 0 1
TEXT 720 800 Left 2 !.meas AC g20 FIND mag(V(lin1)) AT 20
TEXT 720 824 Left 2 !.meas AC g1k FIND mag(V(lin1)) AT 1k
TEXT 720 848 Left 2 !.meas AC g20k FIND mag(V(lin1)) AT 20k
TEXT 720 888 Left 2 ;.tran 0 20m 0 2u
TEXT 720 912 Left 2 ;.noise V(lin1) VIN dec 20 10 100k
TEXT 720 936 Left 2 ;.op
TEXT 720 960 Left 2 ;The lines above starting with a dot are other analyses: remove the semicolon to use one.
